# Security and secrets

## Never

- Commit secrets, tokens, private keys, `.env` contents, or connection strings
- Print full secret values in chat, handoffs, PRs, or logs
- Rotate, rewrite, or chmod secrets automatically
- Embed secrets in webhook URLs or example docs

## Always

- Use environment variables for credentials (outside git)
- Keep `.env` / `.env.*` gitignored; allow only sanitized `.env.example` without real values
- Apply least privilege; do not escalate host access from agent sessions
- Validate inputs on any webhook/API surface (when implementing in product repos)
- Warn if credentials appear in the working tree: report **path + risk**, not values; ask Gio to rotate if exposure is likely

## This repository

- `.gitignore` already excludes `.drafts/`, `.secrets/`, `.env`, `.env.*` (with `!.env.example`)
- No `.env` or credential files were found in-tree at last audit
- Handoffs must contain **no secrets** (`docs/shared-ai-memory/README.md`)

## Sensitive surfaces (external map)

- Ollama on VPS must stay private (`127.0.0.1`)
- Do not disable auth on n8n / MCP / public entrypoints
- `/opt/sc2027/.env` hardening is privileged OPS — document only; do not attempt from this kit alone
